# Project Context

Copy this file to `PROJECT.md`. Replace every `{{REPLACE_ME:*}}` token and
delete optional sections that do not apply. Executable commands and stage lists
belong only in committed `HARNESS/config.env`; this file explains why they are
required, what they cover, and who owns them.

## Required Core

- Project name: `{{REPLACE_ME:PROJECT_NAME}}`
- Purpose and observable outcome: `{{REPLACE_ME:PURPOSE}}`
- Lifecycle: `{{REPLACE_ME:LIFECYCLE}}`
- Accountable owner or role: `{{REPLACE_ME:OWNER}}`
- Shared baseline version: `1.0.0`
- Shared baseline source and maintainer: `{{REPLACE_ME:BASELINE_SOURCE}}`

## Sources of Truth

- Product behavior: `{{REPLACE_ME:PRODUCT_SOURCE}}`
- Architecture and durable decisions: `{{REPLACE_ME:ARCHITECTURE_SOURCE}}`
- API and data contracts: `{{REPLACE_ME:CONTRACT_SOURCE}}`
- Operations or explicit non-applicability: `{{REPLACE_ME:OPERATIONS_SOURCE}}`
- Conflict precedence: `{{REPLACE_ME:SOURCE_PRECEDENCE}}`

## Component Map

| Component | Path | Responsibility | Owner | Runtime/version source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `{{REPLACE_ME:COMPONENT}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:PATH}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:RESPONSIBILITY}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:OWNER}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:RUNTIME}}` |

Also identify generated, vendored, migration, fixture, and deployment paths when
they exist.

## Specification-Driven Development

- SDD mode: `required`
- SDD exemption reason: Not applicable while SDD mode is required.
- SDD exemption owner: Not applicable while SDD mode is required.
- SDD exemption follow-up: Not applicable while SDD mode is required.
- Normative specification location: `SPECIFICATION.md`
- Changes requiring a specification: `{{REPLACE_ME:SDD_SCOPE}}`
- Repository policy for changes that may use committed SDD mode `off`:
  `{{REPLACE_ME:SDD_OFF_SCOPE_OWNER_AND_FOLLOW_UP}}`
- Specification owner: `{{REPLACE_ME:SPEC_OWNER}}`
- Requirements approver: `{{REPLACE_ME:REQUIREMENTS_APPROVER}}`
- Design and test-plan approver: `{{REPLACE_ME:PLAN_APPROVER}}`
- Change ID lifecycle and same-change/new-change decision authority:
  `{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID_LIFECYCLE}}`
- Specification versioning policy:
  `{{REPLACE_ME:SPEC_VERSION_POLICY}}`
- Requirement and acceptance-ID replacement/deprecation policy:
  `{{REPLACE_ME:REQUIREMENT_ID_POLICY}}`
- Investigation and prototype isolation/disposition policy:
  `{{REPLACE_ME:EXPLORATION_POLICY}}`
- Required SDD artifacts: `SPECIFICATION.md`, `SPEC_CHANGELOG.md`,
  `DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md`, `TEST_PLAN.md`, `TRACEABILITY.md`, and
  `plans/<change-id>.md`
- Emergency SDD-off authority, required committed reason, and
  retrospective-spec deadline: `{{REPLACE_ME:SDD_EMERGENCY_POLICY}}`
- SDD conflict precedence: approved specification > approved plan basis and
  approved test plan > tasks > implementation and observed test results >
  descriptive documentation. User and applicable instruction authority still
  take precedence over repository files.
- Material uncertainty protocol: document the issue and evidence, viable
  options and consequences, the recommended option and rationale, and the named
  decision owner before changing the specification or approved plan basis.

## Development and Verification Intent

`HARNESS/config.env` is the executable source of truth. Record only the intent
and boundaries here; do not copy command strings or numeric settings.

- Definition of Done, why each configured stage is required, and which product
  stages may close SDD acceptance evidence: `{{REPLACE_ME:STAGE_INTENT}}`
- Integration/E2E prerequisites and isolated data: `{{REPLACE_ME:TEST_BOUNDARIES}}`
- Security, CI, supply-chain, and deployment gate rationale: `{{REPLACE_ME:GATE_RATIONALE}}`
- Supported developer/CI environments and version files: `{{REPLACE_ME:ENVIRONMENTS}}`
- Harness setting override policy: `committed policy values are authoritative; {{REPLACE_ME:ALLOWED_RUNTIME_OVERRIDES}}`
- Deterministic handoff command: `./HARNESS/harness.sh verify`

## Security and Data

- Data classification: `{{REPLACE_ME:DATA_CLASSIFICATION}}`
- Authentication/authorization authority: `{{REPLACE_ME:AUTHORITY}}`
- Secret-management and redaction rules: `{{REPLACE_ME:SECRET_POLICY}}`
- Dependency and vulnerability policy: `{{REPLACE_ME:DEPENDENCY_POLICY}}`
- Backup, deletion, recovery, and incident owner: `{{REPLACE_ME:RECOVERY_POLICY}}`

## Compatibility and Change Management

- Public interfaces and compatibility promise: `{{REPLACE_ME:COMPATIBILITY}}`
- Migration and deprecation process: `{{REPLACE_ME:MIGRATION}}`
- Governance activation and approval enforcement: `{{REPLACE_ME:GOVERNANCE_POLICY}}`
- Approval roles and independent-review threshold: `{{REPLACE_ME:APPROVAL_ROLES}}`

## Instruction Contract

- Instruction targets checked by Harness: `{{REPLACE_ME:INSTRUCTION_TARGETS}}`
- Instruction compatibility: `{{REPLACE_ME:OPEN_BASELINE_OR_CODEX_EXTENSIONS}}`
- Project-only agent rules: `{{REPLACE_ME:PROJECT_RULES}}`

